  "dataset_type": "Histology",
  "description": "H&E performed after multiplexed (27 antibody) immunofluorescence assay on same section (HBM748.KCTH.488, 5 micron, FFPE). The tissue section is from the right lower lobe of lung of a 1.6-year-old white female (D115)  born at extremely low gestational age with secondary bronchopulmonary dysplasia, pulmonary hypertension and arrested alveolar development. Pathologist review reports: Classic chronic neonatal lung disease/BPD with severe deficient lung growth, lobular remodeling (fibrosis and smooth muscle hyperplasia), reactive airway epithelium and macrophage accumulation, Pulmonary arteriopathy with medial hypertrophy and intimal hyperplasia. Unable to accurately determine radial alveolar count (RAC) due to severe remodeling.",
